*.iml
.gradle/
.gradle-cache/
.idea/
.kotlin/
local.properties
.DS_Store
**/build/
/captures
.externalNativeBuild
.cxx

# Local tooling / agent state
.codex-*
.claude/
.planning/
.serena/
.codegraph/
.zcode/
CLAUDE.md
AGENT_HANDOVER.md

# Signing keys & secrets — NEVER commit these
*.keystore
*.jks
keystore.properties
signing.properties

# Internal planning documents — kept local, never committed. `future_work/` is the core repo's name
# for the same thing; it is listed here too so the same folder name is safe to use anywhere in the
# suite and can never become a committed leak.
future-plan/
audit/
future_work/

# The PRODUCTION Cloudflare Workers — kept local, never committed.
#
# These are the deployments OwnTV's built-in defaults point at, so they carry abuse protection
# (per-client access checks, request budgets, rate limits) that must not be public: publishing it
# would only tell an abuser exactly how to get around it. Root-scoped so `extras/worker/` — the
# public, unprotected self-host copy users are told to deploy — is NOT caught by this.
/worker/

# i18n seed tool run state (batch inputs, IDs, raw results) — never committed
/runs/

# Logcat captures and diagnostic dumps written into the repo root while debugging
# (`adb logcat … | Tee-Object -FilePath .\something.txt`). These routinely contain portal URLs,
# MAC addresses, stream URLs and tokens, so they must never reach a commit. Root-scoped on
# purpose: the baseline profiles under app/src/main/generated/ are .txt and ARE committed.
/*.txt
/*.log

# JVM crash dumps from a Gradle daemon (never worth committing)
hs_err_pid*.log
replay_pid*.log

# Local-only archive (old detailed changelogs etc.), never committed
/archive/
